 "content_notes": "Tone: outrage at the system, never at the man; no mockery of poverty or addiction. Leandro Andrade (convicted; Lockyer v. Andrade, 2003) appears only as a faceless silhouette tagged NOT A LIKENESS. The guard, trial judge, lawyers, reporter, police officer and the young man in the lesson are generic figures, never named; the nine Supreme Court justices are never drawn (nine empty chairs). Kmart is named only as typed text: no logo, sign or store livery. The tape boxes are plain with typed titles only: no Disney or studio artwork or logos. No court seal, badge or insignia. The 'critics' line paraphrases the Ninth Circuit and the Souter dissent; no quote is used. His later release is not claimed (unconfirmed); the parole age is labelled AS SENTENCED. Every card is our own typed graphic. No dialogue is invented. Status verified 2026-10-17.",
